# Moharrik — local development. Copy to .env and fill the two secrets.
# Ports: API :8120, web :3120, Postgres (docker compose) :55470. See README.

# ─── Core ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
APP_ENV=development
APP_URL=http://localhost:8120
ADDR=:8120

# ─── MCP (MH-516) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The URL to hand a connector: a dedicated host with no /api/mcp suffix, e.g.
# https://mcp.moharrik.com. Empty (the default) means "APP_URL + /api/mcp" —
# nothing changes, /api/mcp on the app's own host stays the only entry point.
# Set it to a DIFFERENT host from APP_URL/OAUTH_ISSUER; the same host is
# refused at boot (it would turn "/" on the whole site into the MCP
# transport). The two entry points are separate OAuth audiences: a token
# minted for one is refused at the other (internal/mcp/oauth.go,
# authOAuthForResource). See internal/mcp/public_host.go.
MCP_PUBLIC_URL=

# ─── Database ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Two roles on purpose (README, "Tenancy"):
#   DATABASE_URL      the OWNER role — migrations, auth, tenant resolution, admin MCP
#   APP_DATABASE_URL  the APP role — no superuser, no BYPASSRLS, owns nothing; every
#                     generated route runs on it with row-level security enforced.
# `togo migrate` creates/updates the app role from APP_DATABASE_URL.
DB_DRIVER=pgx
DATABASE_URL=postgres://postgres:postgres@localhost:55470/moharrik?sslmode=disable
APP_DATABASE_URL=postgres://moharrik_app:CHANGE_ME@localhost:55470/moharrik?sslmode=disable

# ─── Client address (rate limits on the public chat widget, MH-377) ─────
# Forwarding headers are believed ONLY from these proxies (IPs/CIDRs, comma
# separated). Unset = loopback only; "none" = believe no header. Any other
# sender's X-Forwarded-For is ignored, because a client can write it itself.
# Production (Cloudflare -> NPM -> container) — see internal/clientip:
#   TRUSTED_PROXIES=10.10.10.100,172.16.0.0/12   (NPM + the docker bridge)
#   CLIENT_IP_HEADER=CF-Connecting-IP            (only if NPM is reachable ONLY via Cloudflare;
#                                                 otherwise keep X-Forwarded-For and add
#                                                 Cloudflare's ranges to TRUSTED_PROXIES)
# Left unset behind a proxy, every visitor shares the proxy's address and the
# per-address limit becomes one bucket for everybody (tighter, never looser).
TRUSTED_PROXIES=
CLIENT_IP_HEADER=X-Forwarded-For

# ─── Logging ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
LOG_LEVEL=info
LOG_FORMAT=text

# ─── i18n / storage ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
LOCALE=en
LOCALE_DIR=lang
STORAGE_DIR=storage
CACHE_DRIVER=memory

# ─── Auth (togo-framework/auth) ──────────────────────────────────────────
AUTH_SECRET=CHANGE_ME_TO_48_RANDOM_CHARS
AUTH_DRIVER=base
AUTH_TTL_HOURS=24
AUTH_MIN_PASSWORD=8
SESSION_DRIVER=cookie
COOKIE_SECURE=
CORS_ORIGINS=http://localhost:3120

# ─── Sign in with Google / Apple (internal/social) ──────────────────────
# Each provider is OFF (no button anywhere) until its variables are set.
# Linking rule: a provider account is found by its subject; a new one is matched
# to an existing account only by a VERIFIED address, and never silently to an
# account that has a password (account_conflict: sign in, then connect it from
# the account page).
#
# Google — the sign-in client (NOT the GOOGLE_INTEGRATIONS_* data client below).
# Authorized redirect URI: {APP_URL}/api/auth/oauth/google/callback
#   https://app.moharrik.com/api/auth/oauth/google/callback
# OAUTH_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
# OAUTH_GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=
# Optional: more audiences a NATIVE Google id_token may carry (POST /api/auth/native/google),
# e.g. the iOS and Android client ids, comma separated. The apps use the browser flow today.
# OAUTH_GOOGLE_AUDIENCES=
# Where a successful sign-in with no ?next= lands (a local path only).
# OAUTH_AFTER_LOGIN=/workspaces
#
# Apple — a Services ID for the web (Return URL {APP_URL}/api/auth/oauth/apple/callback,
# Apple POSTs to it), the app's bundle id(s) for native Sign in with Apple on iOS, and one
# Sign in with Apple key (.p8) from the same team. The key signs the client secret (ES256)
# for the code exchange and the token revocation done on unlink / account deletion.
# APPLE_SERVICES_ID=com.fadymondy.moharrik.web
# APPLE_BUNDLE_IDS=com.fadymondy.moharrik
# APPLE_TEAM_ID=JW9HJH86GC
# APPLE_KEY_ID=
# The .p8 contents (PEM; literal \n accepted) or a path to it. Never commit it.
# APPLE_PRIVATE_KEY=
# APPLE_PRIVATE_KEY_PATH=
#
# GitHub sign-in is not offered.

# ─── Google integrations (MH-439) ────────────────────────────────────────
# Each workspace connects its own Google accounts for Analytics, Search Console
# and YouTube (Settings → Integrations). Unset = the page says Google is not
# configured on this server instead of showing buttons that cannot work.
#
# Deliberately NOT the OAUTH_GOOGLE_* pair above. Those turn on Sign in with
# Google (internal/social), with its own callback ({APP_URL}/api/auth/oauth/google/callback). Separate
# names keep one switch from turning the other on, and let the integrations use
# a client whose consent screen carries the analytics/webmasters/youtube scopes.
# The integration code never reads OAUTH_GOOGLE_*.
# GOOGLE_INTEGRATIONS_CLIENT_ID=
# GOOGLE_INTEGRATIONS_CLIENT_SECRET=
# The callback registered on that client is {PUBLIC_URL or APP_URL}/api/google/oauth/callback:
#   https://app.moharrik.com/api/google/oauth/callback   (production)
#   https://dev.moharrik.com/api/google/oauth/callback   (dev)
# Override only if the public origin differs from both:
# GOOGLE_INTEGRATIONS_REDIRECT_URL=
# DEV/TEST ONLY: one origin standing in for every Google endpoint (the fake in
# internal/google/googletest/fakegoogle). Ignored unless APP_URL is localhost and
# APP_ENV is not production.
# GOOGLE_API_BASE=

# ─── Mail ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Not used in P0: invitations return a one-time link instead of sending email.
MAIL_DRIVER=log

# ─── Account mail (internal/account) ─────────────────────────────────────
# Moharrik's own mail about an account: "confirm your email" and "reset your
# password". Not a workspace's SMTP service. Unset = no account mail, and
# "Forgot password?" is hidden on the web and in the apps (GET /api/auth/methods
# lists password_reset only when this is set). Links open on WEB_URL (else APP_URL).
# MAIL_SMTP_HOST=
# MAIL_SMTP_PORT=587
# MAIL_SMTP_TLS=starttls          # none | starttls | tls (465 implies tls)
# MAIL_SMTP_USERNAME=
# MAIL_SMTP_PASSWORD=
# MAIL_FROM_EMAIL=no-reply@moharrik.com
# MAIL_FROM_NAME=Moharrik

# ─── Hosbah monitoring ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# APM (API traces + exceptions): Hosbah injects OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT / _PROTOCOL=http/json /
# _HEADERS=x-hosbah-key=… / OTEL_SERVICE_NAME into the app's env on each deploy once APM is on
# (internal/telemetry). Unset = no traces. Never commit the hbt_ key.
# RUM (browser page loads, Web Vitals, JS errors): the hbr_ key from Hosbah → app → RUM. It is
# public (every page carries it); empty = no <script> tag.
HOSBAH_URL=https://app.hosbah.com
HOSBAH_RUM_KEY=

# ─── Mahaam feedback ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Moharrik files its own problem reports (the in-app "Report a problem" widget and backend
# panics / 5xx) as issues in its Mahaam project. Empty key = reporting off. Never commit a key.
MAHAAM_URL=https://console.mahaam.app
MAHAAM_FEEDBACK_KEY=
# The Origin Mahaam checks against the key's allowed origins. It must be ON that list (Mahaam →
# project → feedback keys), or every report is refused with 403 (MH-464).
MAHAAM_APP_URL=https://moharrik.com
NEXT_PUBLIC_MAHAAM_EMBED_ORIGIN=https://console.mahaam.app

# Research runs (MH-227): search, read, summarise.
# Each tier is independently optional. Without SEARXNG_URL a run cannot start;
# without FIRECRAWL_* the pages are listed but not read; without AI_PROVIDERS
# they are collected but not summarised, which is a supported way to run this.
SEARXNG_URL=
FIRECRAWL_URL=
FIRECRAWL_API_KEY=
# How many characters of source text one summary may carry. Really a property
# of the MODEL: raise it for a large-context model, lower it for a local 8k one.
RESEARCH_PROMPT_CHARS=24000
# The model. See internal/ai/config.go for the full set.
AI_PROVIDERS=
AI_TASK_DEFAULT=

# ─── Web Push (MH-378) ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Standards Web Push with VAPID (RFC 8292) — no Firebase project involved. The
# browser's push service (FCM for Chrome, Mozilla's for Firefox, WNS for Edge,
# Apple's for Safari) delivers to a member's device when no Moharrik tab is open.
# Generate a pair ONCE per environment and keep it — a new pair invalidates every
# existing subscription, and members would have to enable push again:
#   go run ./cmd/moharrik-admin vapid
# Unset = push is off (the Delivery page says so); the bell, popup, chime and
# desktop notification in an open tab work without it. Never commit a real pair.
VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY=
VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY=
# A contact for the push service operators: mailto:you@example.com or https://…
VAPID_SUBJECT=mailto:alerts@moharrik.com
# The push services the server will POST to (host suffixes, comma separated).
# Unset = FCM, Mozilla, WNS and Apple. This is the SSRF boundary: an endpoint
# comes from a member's browser, so nothing outside this list is ever called.
# PUSH_ALLOWED_HOSTS=

# ─── Native push for the Moharrik apps (docs/apps-plan.md) ──────────────────
# FCM HTTP v1 delivers to the iOS/Android apps (APNs is relayed by Firebase).
# The Firebase project's service-account key: raw JSON or base64 of it, or a
# path in GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS. Unset = native push is off; web push
# and the desktop app (SSE) are unaffected. Never commit a real key.
FCM_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_JSON=
# FCM_PROJECT_ID=
# FCM_DRY_RUN=1

# --- CircleXO hub (sign in with CircleXO, org <-> workspace, hub entitlements, hub MCP tokens) ---
# Everything below is OFF unless CIRCLEXO_ISSUER is set; see docs/circlexo.md. Values come from
# the hub registration and live in the vault, never in the repo.
CIRCLEXO_ISSUER=
CIRCLEXO_APP_ID=
CIRCLEXO_CLIENT_ID=
CIRCLEXO_CLIENT_SECRET=
# Or a private key for private_key_jwt client auth instead of the secret:
# CIRCLEXO_PRIVATE_KEY=
# CIRCLEXO_KEY_ID=
# The hub app API, when it differs from the issuer:
# CIRCLEXO_API_URL=
CIRCLEXO_APP_KEY=
# whsec_... signing secret for webhooks and provision/deprovision calls (required)
CIRCLEXO_WEBHOOK_SECRET=
# Seals the sign-in state cookie. Empty: derived from AUTH_SECRET.
CIRCLEXO_SESSION_KEY=
# Optional. Default: WEB_URL + /auth/circlexo/callback
# CIRCLEXO_REDIRECT_URL=
# Optional. Hub billing page; {slug} is the org slug. Default: <issuer>/orgs/{slug}/billing
# CIRCLEXO_BILLING_URL=
# The public web origin (redirects, post-logout, launch landing). Falls back to APP_URL.
WEB_URL=
